# Working surface, not repo content (Darron's ruling, 2026-08-08 — the tidy-up
# before the Mint 22 hop). These are where builds get staged, probed and diffed;
# they are not the build. Ignoring them is the actual cure for "there seems to be
# lots uncommitted" — most of that noise was never work awaiting a commit.
#   scratchpad/ — held diffs, probes, FULL-file drafts (416K)
#   quarantine/ — the 2026-07-08 /tmp capture rescue (660M of raw typescripts).
#     Committing it would put transient capture into history permanently, which is
#     against DEC-069's grain rather than with it: the rule protects MEMORY from
#     destruction, it does not ask us to version every byte that ever passed through.
#     NOTE: quarantine/ carries its own .gitignore claiming "the manifest + this
#     file are tracked" — they are NOT (git ls-files is empty there). Flagged to
#     Darron; if he wants the RECORD (README.md + MANIFEST.tsv) versioned without
#     the blobs, that is a negation rule and a separate deliberate act.
scratchpad/
quarantine/
